WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.269
Every shop in the metro is competing

00:00:02.269 --> 00:00:03.548
for attention.

00:00:03.548 --> 00:00:05.769
Meet Leo, a furniture merchant.

00:00:05.769 --> 00:00:07.721
For days, he has struggled to bring

00:00:07.721 --> 00:00:09.067
customers back.

00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:11.691
He checks product interest, sales records and

00:00:11.691 --> 00:00:13.778
payments, but still can't tell who to

00:00:13.778 --> 00:00:15.595
contact or what to offer.

00:00:15.717 --> 00:00:17.592
Could AI do this for Leo?

00:00:18.192 --> 00:00:19.717
Meet Market Metro.

00:00:19.792 --> 00:00:22.917
Its ontology connects shoppers, products and payments

00:00:22.967 --> 00:00:25.317
into one shared map, giving the agent

00:00:25.417 --> 00:00:27.417
meaningful evidence to work with.

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:30.175
The ontology maps each business question to

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.100
the right training examples.

00:00:32.175 --> 00:00:35.500
Product recommendations and general inquiries follow separate

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:38.925
paths, while later payment outcomes supply labels,

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.275
not predictors.

00:00:40.417 --> 00:00:43.642
Now follow one saved reactivation campaign.

00:00:43.692 --> 00:00:46.742
The agent analyzes demand, chooses twenty eight

00:00:46.792 --> 00:00:49.492
days of history, and fits two models.

00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:51.667
A verifier tests the campaign before it

00:00:51.717 --> 00:00:53.042
reaches shoppers.

00:00:53.183 --> 00:00:54.783
The first idea doesn't get a free

00:00:54.833 --> 00:00:55.758
pass.

00:00:55.833 --> 00:00:58.383
A verifier tests both rankings in separate

00:00:58.433 --> 00:01:00.683
development markets and selects the one that

00:01:00.733 --> 00:01:03.258
earns more while protecting merchants.

00:01:03.383 --> 00:01:06.108
On day thirty five, the selected recommendation

00:01:06.183 --> 00:01:07.683
reaches our shopper.

00:01:07.758 --> 00:01:09.583
They buy a ninety six dollar side

00:01:09.633 --> 00:01:12.023
table, and it arrives the next day;

00:01:12.098 --> 00:01:15.223
fixed rules left that same request unfilled.

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:17.684
We mirror that order once through PayPal

00:01:17.684 --> 00:01:18.644
Sandbox.

00:01:18.644 --> 00:01:21.047
The completed capture records the fee and

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:23.792
merchant proceeds, then returns a receipt that

00:01:23.792 --> 00:01:25.370
links all the way back to the

00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:26.400
purchase.

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:29.463
Against fixed rules, sixteen more purchases were

00:01:29.463 --> 00:01:31.059
completed and kept.

00:01:31.059 --> 00:01:33.694
That's two thousand three hundred forty five

00:01:33.694 --> 00:01:35.983
dollars in extra payment volume, over a

00:01:35.983 --> 00:01:38.896
thousand dollars in merchant contribution, and a

00:01:38.896 --> 00:01:41.601
hundred fifteen dollars in modeled PayPal net

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:42.850
after AI cost.

00:01:42.983 --> 00:01:45.171
Judges can follow the whole trail in

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.139
A G Grid, from model training and

00:01:47.139 --> 00:01:49.837
the agent's decision to the PayPal receipt,

00:01:49.837 --> 00:01:52.608
instead of taking the result on trust.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:55.625
Market Metro turns observed activity into tested

00:01:55.675 --> 00:01:59.400
campaigns and traceable payments: agentic commerce that

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:00.275
learns.
